    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0062" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg52"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.94/295: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Leahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-02-01T15:00:00-05:00">February 1, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>104. Your 131, January 30, Section 1. The Department has sent a telegram to the
                    Consulate at Saigon reading in part as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Rubber Reserve Company<anchor n="72" xml:id="d52-f1"/> is prepared
                            to accept offers for any amount of available rubber within its price
                            limit and under terms <pb facs="0063" n="53" xml:id="pg53"/> similar to
                            those embodied in previous contracts. It will also consider offers
                            covering production for the coming year. You are therefore requested to
                            discuss this matter with the Government General in an endeavor to
                            ascertain whether or not it is possible to effect such a contract under
                            the terms indicated. If this does not appear feasible, the question of
                            alternative terms should be discussed and reported at the earliest
                            possible moment.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d52-f1" n="72" xml:id="d52-f1-content">
                <p>The Rubber Reserve Company, a component of the Federal Loan Agency, was set up on
                    June 28, 1940, under authority of the Reconstruction Finance Corporation Act of
                    March 9, 1933 (48 Stat. 6), as amended on June 25, 1940 (54 Stat 572).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
